<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela disclosed a $237.5 billion debt pile and began a large restructuring while the United States signed a security cooperation pact with the interim Venezuelan government, after which a U.S. marine died falling overboard during a Caribbean operation linked to the renewed ties. The Senate is probing JD Vance for allegedly steering a Venezuelan oil license to Vitol and another senator’s role in the same deal, while Citi is weighing a market re-entry after a five-year exit. Venezuelan authorities later declared the security pact null and void, illegal gold mining continues, and Eni and Repsol pledged a $2 billion joint-venture investment. According to UCDP, there were 2 battle-related deaths in 2007.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxOZk56U1ppNndqeTVWb2FvZ1ktaVRZTEx0WENYTEFCMVR2Q2huWnJBbG11ek5IUVVmaVJqUjItSDNmZDlaTVNGNjhoa09Wd1E1OXNKbG85WGVTZGpvVVVSYW1iZEc0alF4Q3ZFb1hqYXdrVFd5SjVjbnp0MDZlZVNZam5HY1M2czV1SHFSV0dIcUFvV3U2Q1FhT0I0MGF2UzlPd3FhRXVR?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiSEFVX3lxTE05RUgxMXB2Qm9ia3NEQi05a1V3bG4tbmxscjh5Q1hQc242YXhaSVg0RldkYlRpcEJNdlhTLWI4Zm1qNnBZNjNzYQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Dawn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxNSnBhS2YxRk5nTjRFbDJON0ROb19SVEYzc2dGYUpnb0ozdzV0Y2p2eHRjMVlYd3p3M09lam1qTHN2dkNhVDhsZmVvNUE3NXg3dFlCOWh4NUNzVXNqUmt4LVBDRFNCdDNGdlU0ak9hVTY1c1J4VXJ4a2stZndwbzE3b2QxLWxjMlJydmNkUlJDTTRDTmdDV21PS2hraVRUT0pLM29OLXJtZV9kaVhqTWlRc2tWM25tMFdNUnR0RXU3TQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxQcEtHbDFTdktXYlpLTjcwc2VlcHFBS1RFd3YtcXgxM282NlVETEIyYTFsSzBzUGJZMm9KZWVGZ3BFQm9vUXRUWm5Ea3VMcHpuWWowVVhEeHE1aTR2MkFLTENHcjJjd2RGSm5GT2FlV2NfVHdLMDVyOEVxMW1SMnJJbG5ORkVxXzlpcUZaMXgzVUdtNE9wd3o4UExNOXQ